    "title" : "Avoid Iteration Over ls Output",
    "description" : "This rule detects when scripts iterate over the output of the 'ls' command, which is fragile and error-prone.",
    "explanation" : "## iteration-over-ls-output\nIterating over ls output is fragile. Use globs, e.g. 'dir/*' instead of '$(ls dir)'.",
