    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Instantiating RegionInfo with Two-Character Culture Codes for Inter-Process Communication",
    "description" : "Detects RegionInfo objects instantiated with two-letter ISO region codes that are used in inter-process communication or persistence, which can cause errors.",
    "explanation" : "## correctness-regioninfo-interop\nPotential inter-process write of RegionInfo $RI via $PIPESTREAM $P that was instantiated with a two-character culture code $REGION.  Per .NET documentation, if you want to persist a RegionInfo object or communicate it between processes, you should instantiate it by using a full culture name rather than a two-letter ISO region code.",
