  {
    "id" : "go.gorilla.security.audit.websocket-missing-origin-check.websocket-missing-origin-check",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "CSRF",
    "title" : "Enforce Origin Header Check in Gorilla WebSocket Handshake",
    "description" : "Ensure the Origin header in the HTTP WebSocket handshake is validated to accept connections only from trusted origin domains.",
    "explanation" : "## websocket-missing-origin-check\nThe Origin header in the HTTP WebSocket handshake is used to guarantee that the connection accepted by the WebSocket is from a trusted origin domain. Failure to enforce can lead to Cross Site Request Forgery (CSRF). As per \"gorilla/websocket\" documentation: \"A CheckOrigin function should carefully validate the request origin to prevent cross-site request forgery.\"",
