    "description" : "Detects file permissions set to more than 0600, which is usually unnecessary and violates the principle of least privilege.",
    "explanation" : "## incorrect-default-permission\nDetected file permissions that are set to more than `0600` (user/owner can read and write). Setting file permissions to higher than `0600` is most likely unnecessary and violates the principle of least privilege. Instead, set permissions to be `0600` or less for os.Chmod, os.Mkdir, os.OpenFile, os.MkdirAll, and ioutil.WriteFile",
