    "title" : "Enforce Minimum TLS Version in SSL Configuration",
    "description" : "Ensures that the TLS configuration explicitly sets a minimum TLS version to avoid using insecure older versions.",
    "explanation" : "## missing-ssl-minversion\n`MinVersion` is missing from this TLS configuration.  By default, TLS 1.2 is currently used as the minimum when acting as a client, and TLS 1.0 when acting as a server. General purpose web applications should default to TLS 1.3 with all other protocols disabled.  Only where it is known that a web server must support legacy clients with unsupported an insecure browsers (such as Internet Explorer 10), it may be necessary to enable TLS 1.0 to provide support. Add `MinVersion: tls.VersionTLS13' to the TLS configuration to bump the minimum version to TLS 1.3.",
