  {
    "id" : "go_leak_rule-pprof-endpoint",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "InsecureModulesLibraries",
    "title" : "Avoid Exposing Go pprof Profiling Endpoint",
    "description" : "Detects usage of Go's built-in profiling service via the net/http/pprof package which exposes the /debug/pprof endpoint without authentication.",
    "explanation" : "## go_leak_rule-pprof-endpoint\nGo has a built in profiling service that is enabled by starting an HTTP server with\n`net/http/pprof` imported. The `/debug/pprof` endpoint does not require any\nauthentication and can be accessed by anonymous users. This profiling endpoint\ncan leak sensitive information and should not be enabled in production.\n\nTo remediate this, remove the `net/http/pprof` import from the file.",
