    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "SSL",
    "title" : "Avoid Accepting User-Installed CA Certificates for Domain in Network Security Config",
    "description" : "Checks if the Network Security Config is set to accept user-installed Certificate Authorities (CAs) for a domain, which may pose security risks.",
    "explanation" : "## nsc-allows-user-ca-certs-for-domain\nThe Network Security Config is set to accept user-installed CAs for the domain `$DOMAIN`. Evaluate if this is necessary for your app, and disable it if appropriate. (To hide this warning, set `xmlns:tools=\"http://schemas.android.com/tools\" tools:ignore=\"AcceptsUserCertificates\"` as parameters to your `<network-security-config>`)",
