    "subCategory" : "InputValidation",
    "title" : "Detect Tainted LDAP Query from HTTP Request",
    "description" : "Detects when input from an HTTPServletRequest is directly used in an LDAP query, which can lead to LDAP injection vulnerabilities.",
    "explanation" : "## tainted-ldapi-from-http-request\nDetected input from a HTTPServletRequest going into an LDAP query. This could lead to LDAP injection if the input is not properly sanitized, which could result in attackers modifying objects in the LDAP tree structure. Ensure data passed to an LDAP query is not controllable or properly sanitize the data.",
