    "description" : "This rule detects the use of non-primitive classes in Java RMI which may lead to insecure deserialization vulnerabilities.",
    "explanation" : "## server-dangerous-class-deserialization\nUsing a non-primitive class with Java RMI may be an insecure deserialization vulnerability. Depending on the underlying implementation. This object could be manipulated by a malicious actor allowing them to execute code on your system. Instead, use an integer ID to look up your object, or consider alternative serialization schemes such as JSON.",
