    "explanation" : "## server-dangerous-object-deserialization\nUsing an arbitrary object ('$PARAMTYPE $PARAM') with Java RMI is an insecure deserialization vulnerability. This object can be manipulated by a malicious actor allowing them to execute code on your system. Instead, use an integer ID to look up your object, or consider alternative serialization schemes such as JSON.",
