    "id" : "java.spring.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
    "level" : "Error",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "SQLInjection",
    "title" : "Avoid Tainted SQL String Construction",
    "description" : "Detects when user data is directly used in manually-constructed SQL strings, which can lead to SQL injection vulnerabilities.",
    "explanation" : "## tainted-sql-string\nUser data flows into this manually-constructed SQL string. User data can be safely inserted into SQL strings using prepared statements or an object-relational mapper (ORM). Manually-constructed SQL strings is a possible indicator of SQL injection, which could let an attacker steal or manipulate data from the database. Instead, use prepared statements (`connection.PreparedStatement`) or a safe library.",
