    "id" : "kotlin_crypto_rule-CipherECBMode",
    "level" : "Error",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "Cryptography",
    "title" : "Avoid Using Cipher ECB Mode",
    "description" : "This rule detects usage of the Electronic Code Book (ECB) cipher mode which does not provide good confidentiality for encrypted data.",
    "explanation" : "## kotlin_crypto_rule-CipherECBMode\nAn authentication cipher mode which provides better confidentiality of the encrypted data\nshould be used instead of Electronic Code Book (ECB) mode, which does not provide good\nconfidentiality. Specifically, ECB mode produces the same output for the same input each time.\nThis allows an attacker to intercept and replay the data.",
