    "title" : "Avoid Weak TLS Protocols by Disallowing HostnameVerifier that Accepts Any Host",
    "description" : "Detects usage of HostnameVerifier implementations that accept any host, which weakens TLS security by allowing certificate reuse across hosts.",
    "explanation" : "## kotlin_crypto_rule-WeakTLSProtocol\nA HostnameVerifier that accept any host are often use because of certificate\nreuse on many hosts. As a consequence, this is vulnerable to Man-in-the-middleattacks\nattacks since the client will trust any certificate.",
    "enabled" : false,
