    "id" : "python.django.correctness.string-field-null-checks.no-null-string-field",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Using null=True on String-Based Django Fields",
    "description" : "Avoid using null=True on string-based Django model fields such as CharField and TextField.",
    "explanation" : "## no-null-string-field\nAvoid using null on string-based fields such as CharField and TextField. If a string-based field has null=True, that means it has two possible values for \"no data\": NULL, and the empty string. In most cases, it's redundant to have two possible values for \"no data;\" the Django convention is to use the empty string, not NULL.",
