  {
    "id" : "python.flask.security.injection.tainted-url-host.tainted-url-host",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "SSL",
    "title" : "Avoid Tainted URL Host in Flask",
    "description" : "Detects when user-controlled data is used in the host portion of a manually constructed URL in Flask applications, which can lead to server-side request forgery (SSRF).",
    "explanation" : "## tainted-url-host\nUser data flows into the host portion of this manually-constructed URL. This could allow an attacker to send data to their own server, potentially exposing sensitive data such as cookies or authorization information sent with this request. They could also probe internal servers or other resources that the server running this code can access. (This is called server-side request forgery, or SSRF.) Do not allow arbitrary hosts. Instead, create an allowlist for approved hosts, or hardcode the correct host.",
