    "subCategory" : "XSS",
    "title" : "Detect Jinja2 Environment with Autoescaping Disabled",
    "description" : "Detects when a Jinja2 environment has autoescaping disabled, which can lead to security vulnerabilities when rendering templates in a web context.",
    "explanation" : "## incorrect-autoescape-disabled\nDetected a Jinja2 environment with 'autoescaping' disabled. This is dangerous if you are rendering to a browser because this allows for cross-site scripting (XSS) attacks. If you are in a web context, enable 'autoescaping' by setting 'autoescape=True.' You may also consider using 'jinja2.select_autoescape()' to only enable automatic escaping for certain file extensions.",
