    "title" : "Avoid SQL Injection in asyncpg Queries",
    "description" : "Detects string concatenation with non-literal variables in asyncpg Python SQL statements, which can lead to SQL injection vulnerabilities.",
    "explanation" : "## asyncpg-sqli\nDetected string concatenation with a non-literal variable in a asyncpg Python SQL statement. This could lead to SQL injection if the variable is user-controlled and not properly sanitized. In order to prevent SQL injection, use parameterized queries or prepared statements instead. You can create parameterized queries like so: 'conn.fetch(\"SELECT $1 FROM table\", value)'. You can also create prepared statements with 'Connection.prepare': 'stmt = conn.prepare(\"SELECT $1 FROM table\"); await stmt.fetch(user_value)'",
