    "subCategory" : "InsecureModulesLibraries",
    "title" : "Use defusedcsv Instead of csv for CSV Generation",
    "description" : "Detects usage of the built-in csv module for generating CSV files and recommends using defusedcsv to prevent CSV formula injection attacks.",
    "explanation" : "## use-defusedcsv\nDetected the generation of a CSV file using the built-in `csv` module. If user data is used to generate the data in this file, it is possible that an attacker could inject a formula when the CSV is imported into a spreadsheet application that runs an attacker script, which could steal data from the importing user or, at worst, install malware on the user's computer. `defusedcsv` is a drop-in replacement with the same API that will attempt to mitigate formula injection attempts. You can use `defusedcsv` instead of `csv` to safely generate CSVs.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
