    "title" : "Enforce Setting Timeout on Requests Calls",
    "description" : "Detects 'requests' library calls in Python that do not have a timeout set.",
    "explanation" : "## use-timeout\nDetected a 'requests' call without a timeout set. By default, 'requests' calls wait until the connection is closed. This means a 'requests' call without a timeout will hang the program if a response is never received. Consider setting a timeout for all 'requests'.",
