  {
    "id" : "scala_crypto_rule-CipherPaddingOracle",
    "level" : "Error",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "Cryptography",
    "title" : "Avoid CBC Mode with PKCS5Padding to Prevent Padding Oracle Attacks",
    "description" : "Detects usage of CBC mode with PKCS5Padding which is vulnerable to padding oracle attacks.",
    "explanation" : "## scala_crypto_rule-CipherPaddingOracle\nThis specific mode of CBC with PKCS5Padding is susceptible to padding oracle attacks. An\nadversary could potentially decrypt the message if the system exposed the difference between\nplaintext with invalid padding or valid padding. The distinction between valid and invalid\npadding is usually revealed through distinct error messages being returned for each condition.",
