    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "InputValidation",
    "title" : "Prevent LDAP Injection",
    "description" : "Ensures that all inputs passed to an LDAP query are handled safely to prevent LDAP injection vulnerabilities.",
    "explanation" : "## scala_inject_rule-LDAPInjection\nJust like SQL, all inputs passed to an LDAP query need to be passed in safely. Unfortunately,\nLDAP doesn't have prepared statement interfaces like SQL. Therefore, the primary defense\nagainst LDAP injection is strong input validation of any untrusted data before including it in\nan LDAP query.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 15,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Scala"
      }
    ]
