    "subCategory" : "FileAccess",
    "title" : "Avoid Absolute Path Traversal in HTTP Request Parameters",
    "description" : "Detects when HTTP request parameters are used to construct file pathnames without properly neutralizing absolute path sequences, potentially allowing access outside restricted directories.",
    "explanation" : "## scala_inject_rule-SpotbugsPathTraversalAbsolute\n\"The software uses an HTTP request parameter to construct a pathname that should be within a\nrestricted directory, but it does not properly neutralize absolute path sequences such as\n\"/abs/path\" that can resolve to a location that is outside of that directory. See\nhttp://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/36.html for more information.\"",
