    "explanation" : "## aws-sns-topic-unencrypted\nThe AWS SNS topic is unencrypted. The SNS topic messages could be read if compromised. The AWS KMS encryption key protects topic contents. To create your own, create a aws_kms_key resource or use the ARN string of a key in your account.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Terraform"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "terraform.aws.security.aws-sqs-queue-policy-wildcard-action.aws-sqs-queue-policy-wildcard-action",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "InsecureModulesLibraries",
    "title" : "Avoid Wildcard Actions in AWS SQS Queue Policies",
    "description" : "This rule detects the use of wildcard (*) in the action field of AWS SQS queue policies, which grants overly broad permissions.",
    "explanation" : "## aws-sqs-queue-policy-wildcard-action\nWildcard used in your SQS queue policy action. SQS queue policies should always grant least privilege - that is, only grant the permissions required to perform a specific task. Implementing least privilege is important to reducing security risks and reducing the effect of errors or malicious intent.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Terraform"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "terraform.aws.security.aws-sqs-queue-policy-wildcard-principal.aws-sqs-queue-policy-wildcard-principal",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "Auth",
    "title" : "Avoid Wildcard Principal in AWS SQS Queue Policy",
    "description" : "Detects usage of wildcard (*) in the principal field of AWS SQS queue policies, which grants access to all users including anonymous ones.",
    "explanation" : "## aws-sqs-queue-policy-wildcard-principal\nWildcard used in your SQS queue policy principal. This grants access to all users, including anonymous users (public access). Unless you explicitly require anyone on the internet to be able to read or write to your queue, limit principals, actions and resources to what you need according to least privilege.",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Terraform"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "terraform.aws.security.aws-sqs-queue-unencrypted.aws-sqs-queue-unencrypted",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "InsecureStorage",
    "title" : "Enforce Encryption on AWS SQS Queues",
    "description" : "This rule detects AWS SQS queues that are created without server-side encryption enabled.",
    "explanation" : "## aws-sqs-queue-unencrypted\nThe AWS SQS queue contents are unencrypted. The data could be read if compromised. Enable server-side encryption for your queue using SQS-managed encryption keys (SSE-SQS), or using your own AWS KMS key (SSE-KMS).",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
      {
        "name" : "Terraform"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
