    "category" : "Security",
    "subCategory" : "SSL",
    "title" : "Enforce use of secure TLS policy for Azure Storage",
    "description" : "This rule ensures that the minimum TLS version for Azure Storage accounts is set to TLS 1.2 to avoid using older, less secure TLS versions 1.0 and 1.1.",
    "explanation" : "## storage-use-secure-tls-policy\nAzure Storage currently supports three versions of the TLS protocol: 1.0, 1.1, and 1.2. Azure Storage uses TLS 1.2 on public HTTPS endpoints, but TLS 1.0 and TLS 1.1 are still supported for backward compatibility. This check will warn if the minimum TLS is not set to TLS1_2.",
